---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'

const effectiveDate = new Date(2026, 10, 5) // November 5, 2026

const formattedEffectiveDate = effectiveDate.toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
	year: 'numeric',
	month: 'long',
	day: 'numeric',
})
---

<Layout
	title='Jellify - Privacy Policy'
	description='How Jellify handles your data.'
>
	<main>
		<article>
			<a class='back' href='/'>← Jellify</a>

			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class='meta'>Effective {formattedEffectiveDate}</p>

			<p>
				Jellify is a free, open source music player for Jellyfin. It's built by volunteers,
				it has no accounts of its own, and it isn't in the business of collecting your data.
				This policy explains how Jellify handles your data - on your device, on this website,
				and optionally sent to GlitchTip for error reporting if enabled.
			</p>

			<h2>Your Jellyfin server</h2>
			<p>
				Jellify connects directly to the Jellyfin server you choose. Your music library,
				playlists, favorites, playback history, and lyrics all come from and are sent to
				<em>your</em> server, not to us. How that data is handled is up to whoever runs the
				server. If that's you, it stays with you.
			</p>

			<h2>Your device data</h2>
			<p>To keep you signed in and remember your preferences, the app stores the following on your device:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your Jellyfin server address</li>
				<li>Your Jellyfin account&apos;s username</li>
				<li>
					An access token issued by your server. Your password is sent to your server when you
					sign in and is not stored by the app.
				</li>
				<li>Your app settings</li>
				<li>Cached library information and artwork, so the app loads quickly and without an active internet connection</li>
				<li>Any music you choose to download for offline playback</li>
			</ul>
			<p>This data never leaves your device except to talk to your own Jellyfin server.</p>

			<h2>Error reporting</h2>
			<p class='meta'>Optional, and off by default</p>
			<p>
				Jellify can send crash and error reports to help us find and fix bugs. This uses
				&nbsp;<a href='https://glitchtip.com'>GlitchTip</a>, an open source error tracking
				service, and is <strong>turned off by default</strong>. Nothing is sent unless you turn
				on <em>Send Analytics</em> in Settings, and you can turn it off at any
				time.
			</p>
			<p>When it's on, reports may include:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>The error message and where in the app it happened</li>
				<li>Your device model, operating system version, and app version</li>
				<li>Which screens you visited and recent app log messages leading up to the error</li>
				<li>A small sample of performance data</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Reports are configured not to include personal information such as your IP address
				or username. GlitchTip's handling of this data is described in its
				&nbsp;<a href='https://glitchtip.com/legal/privacy'>privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Other network requests</h2>
			<p>
				The app's <em>About</em> and <em>Settings</em> screens load the list of Jellify's supporters from
				<code>patrons.jellify.app</code>. This request doesn't include any information about you
				or your library.
			</p>

			<h2>No ads, no tracking, no selling</h2>
			<p>
				Jellify has no advertising, no third-party analytics, and no tracking across apps or
				websites. We don't sell or share your data, because we don't have it nor do we care to collect it.
			</p>

			<h2>This website</h2>
			<p>
				jellify.app doesn't use cookies, analytics, or tracking scripts. It's hosted on
				Cloudflare, which processes basic request information (like your IP address) to serve
				and protect the site, as described in
				&nbsp;<a href='https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/'>Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
			<p>
				Signing out of Jellify or uninstalling the app removes everything it stored on your
				device.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				Jellify doesn't knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children
				under 13.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, we'll update it here and change the effective date above to {formattedEffectiveDate}.
				Its full history is public in this website's &nbsp;
				<a href='https://github.com/Jellify-Music/Website'>GitHub repository</a>.
			</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		padding: 3rem 1rem 4rem;
	}

	article {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.back {
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		font-size: 2.5rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		line-height: 1.1;
	}

	.meta {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--neutral);
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	li + li {
		margin-top: 0.25rem;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--primary);
	}

	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
		border-radius: 4px;
		background-color: var(--background-50);
	}
</style>
